ass-through or billing-integrity refund is due. Both sides' claims to that effect are accepted. (c) The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes (113 fixes, 10 s sample interval, 100.0% coverage, max gap 0.0 s), so no POL-RD-07(a)-(c) limb fires and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged; the rider's and driver's clean-trace claims are accepted. (d) No POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires: trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown (all TRP-02817); no timestamps disagree by more than 10 minutes or run backwards; the computed refund (zero) does not exceed $150.00 or charged_total; and every charge line has a counterpart. The case is ripe for a ruling, not an escalation.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S ROAD-WORKS EXPLANATION. The driver's counterparty statement ('Minor detour because of a road works sign') is not needed to decide this case, because no deviation is established. I nevertheless record that no traffic advisory is on file for this trip: EV-ADVIS-02817-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so the POL-RD-03 comparison cannot be run and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08 (POL-RD-13). Because the driver cited no advisory evidence ID, the absent artifact is a gap in the bundle and not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged on that ground.\n\nNO DRIVER COMPENSATION. POL-RD-04's unbilled-distance limb needs the billed distance to fall short of the trace by more than 1.0 km; the ledger bills 14.4 km against a trace of 14.39 km, a 0.01 km difference, so no compensation is owed. No POL-RD-06 pattern is present (deviation_flags_90d 0 against complete_trips_90d 174, and the excess is not MATERIAL), so no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral arises. No exculpatory clause is available to the driver: there is no chat log at all (EV-CHAT-02817, 0 messages) so POL-RD-04 cannot be invoked, no pickup/dropoff amendment is recorded so POL-RD-05 does not apply, and the vehicle type is RYDE_X not RYDE_POOL so POL-RD-12 does not apply.\n\nPROFILE FIELDS. Only the fields POL-GEN-01 names for a test may be used: deviation_flags_90d / completed_trips_90d (POL-RD-06) and deviation_claims_60d / deviation_claims_60d_substantiated (POL-RD-08). Both are 0 on their respective tests here. Rating, account age, lifetime trips, cancellation rates and prior dispute counters are context only and are used for nothing; the kept rider claim that mentions them is doing so only to disclaim them, which is proper.\n\nUnder POL-GEN-03, NO_ACTION is party-relative: on this rider-filed dispute it leaves fare_breakdown.payment_status CHARGED and the $20.64 in place, with refund_issued_sgd unchanged at 0.0. Confidence 0.9: the deciding facts (trace distance 14.39 km and optimal distance 12.0 km) are carried by EV-GPS-02817 and EV-TRIP-02817, both at weight_multiplier 1.0."
